// ============================================================================
//  mod_locations.zone
//
//  v1.15.0 cut this file down hard. It used to carry 31 menu/loadscreen
//  materials, the Buried zombie aitypes and their 118 xmodels, the Mob of the
//  Dead player characters, the Buried ghost animtree and the custom gametype
//  rawfiles - all of it supporting the ported survival locations and custom
//  gamemodes, which are gone.
//
//  DINER is the one added location the mod still ships, so only what Diner
//  needs is left, plus one unrelated stock gap worth keeping.
//
//  🛑 A MATERIAL HERE IS ONLY HALF THE ASSET. Declaring it gives mod.ff the
//  material and an image *header*. T6 does NOT store pixel data in the
//  fastfile - it loads that from a loose .iwi at runtime. So every image these
//  materials reference must ALSO exist in the project's images\ folder, which
//  pack_iwd.ps1 packs into mod.iwd. Ship only half and the material resolves,
//  the image asset exists, and it draws BLACK. build.bat syncs
//  zone_assets\images\ -> images\ so the two cannot drift.
// ============================================================================
>game,T6

// --- Diner: lobby preview + loading screen ---
material,menu_zm_transit_zsurvival_diner
material,loadscreen_zm_transit_zstandard_diner

// Mob of the Dead played as CLASSIC derives loadscreen_zm_prison_zclassic_prison,
// which stock never shipped. Nothing to do with the survival locations - without
// it MOTD classic simply has no loading screen - so it stays.
material,loadscreen_zm_prison_zclassic_prison

// ============================================================================
//  MODELS DINER SPAWNS THAT ITS MAP DOES NOT SHIP
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Both exist in the stock game, but only inside the per-gametype "so_" files:
//      p6_zm_buildable_bench_tarp           so_zsurvival_zm_transit,
//                                           so_zencounter_zm_{transit,prison}
//      zm_collision_transit_diner_survival  so_zsurvival_zm_transit,
//                                           so_zencounter_zm_transit, zm_transit_dr
//
//  TranZit is the one map in the game that ships a so_zsurvival file, so on
//  TranZit these would resolve anyway - but pulling them into mod.ff registers
//  them globally and costs nothing.
// ============================================================================
xmodel,p6_zm_buildable_bench_tarp
xmodel,zm_collision_transit_diner_survival

// ============================================================================
//  WUNDERFIZZ  -  the real Origins machine, on every map
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  scripts\zm\wunderfizz.gsc places a Der Wunderfizz on all six maps. Upstream
//  could only do this with a JUGGERNOG model standing in, because it ships as a
//  loose script and cannot add assets. This is a real mod with a fastfile, so it
//  uses the actual machine.
//
//  Per the Unlinker, every one of these lives ONLY in zm_tomb.ff:
//      xmodel  p6_zm_vending_diesel_magic          the machine
//      fx      maps/zombie_tomb/fx_tomb_dieselmagic_on   the swirl it plays
//      xmodel  t6_wpn_zmb_perk_bottle_bear_world   the teddy on relocate
//  build_ff.bat already --loads zm_tomb.ff, so the Linker copies them out of it.
//
//  🛑 FX ARE A SPECIAL CASE. OpenAssetTools can neither compile nor dump an
//  FxEffectDef (its matrix lists it ❌/❌), so this fx CANNOT come from a raw
//  source file - it only resolves by being copied out of a --load'ed fastfile
//  that owns it at scope=top, which zm_tomb.ff does. If that copy ever fails the
//  link, do not go looking for a .efx to add: the answer is the --load, not a
//  source file. See the starter kit's §5.
//
//  🛑 The machine's IMAGES are DLC4 assets. A fastfile stores image headers, not
//  pixels - those come from the ipaks at runtime. If Origins' textures are not in
//  an ipak the other maps mount, the machine will draw untextured/black off
//  Origins even though it spawns correctly. Unverified; check it in game.
// ============================================================================
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  ✅ v1.23.0 - THE REAL MACHINE, REBUILT UNDER MOD-PRIVATE NAMES.
//
//  v1.22.0 removed "xmodel,p6_zm_vending_diesel_magic" because declaring it made
//  mod.ff OWN Origins' Pack-a-Punch monolith textures (108 colliding assets, a
//  garbled Origins HUD and a dead generator indicator). That diagnosis stands -
//  do NOT re-add the stock name. What follows is the rebuild it recommended.
//
//  This one line pulls in a whole chain that is built from source in
//  zone_assets\ and shares no NAME with anything the game ships, so the
//  collision cannot happen:
//      xmodel    qolwf_vending_diesel_magic
//        -> material mc/mtl_qolwf_vending_diesel_magic{,_acc,_ball,_logo}
//                    mc/mtl_qolwf_tm_{crystal,monolith_rock,science_glass}
//        -> image    qolwf_*   (23, from zone_assets\images\*.iwi)
//  Nothing here is resolved out of zm_tomb.ff, so the --load of that file is now
//  only needed by the Electric Cherry chain.
//
//  🛑 THE MESH MUST BE GLB. The Linker cannot compile .xmodel_bin or
//  .XMODEL_EXPORT for T6 - an untouched dump of a stock model fails with
//  "Failure while trying to load model for lod 0". Dump with
//  "Unlinker --model-format GLB" and point the lods at the .glb.
//
//  🛑 The material renames inside the .glb are byte-length-preserving on purpose
//  (p6_zm_tm_ -> qolwf_tm_, p6_zm_vending_ -> qolwf_vending_). A glTF chunk
//  stores its own length, so a rename that changes the size corrupts the file.
//
//  🛑 And these images need REAL PIXELS, unlike every other image in this zone.
//  A material declared here normally borrows the game's own .iwi at runtime; a
//  mod-private image name matches nothing, so zone_assets\images\qolwf_*.iwi
//  must exist (build.bat syncs them into images\ -> mod.iwd). They were rebuilt
//  from the workspace texture dumps rather than the ipaks, which OAT cannot read.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
xmodel,qolwf_vending_diesel_magic

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  ...and the BALL SPIN, same trick. v1.23.0 restored the model but left the
//  machine standing still; these are the animation half.
//
//  🛑 Both the animtree and the xanims are renamed. xanim assets are identified
//  purely by FILENAME (nothing inside references their own name), and the .atr
//  is plain text listing the anim names - so unlike an fx, both rename cleanly
//  and collide with nothing. Verified: the Linker compiles all five from disk.
//
//  🛑 A rawfile only reaches the game through mod.ff - mod.iwd serves scripts
//  but NOT .atr/.txt/.asd - so the animtree MUST be declared here.
//
//  🛑 Declaring the tree only makes the ASSET exist. wunderfizz.gsc must also
//  call scriptmodelsuseanimtree( #animtree ) at runtime or every map dies on
//  load with "Unrecognized animtree". v1.21.0 shipped without it and did not
//  boot. See the comment above main() in wunderfizz.gsc.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
rawfile,animtrees/qolwf_perk_random.atr
xanim,qolwf_diesel_turn_on
xanim,qolwf_diesel_turn_off
xanim,qolwf_diesel_on_idle
xanim,qolwf_diesel_ballspin_loop

// REMOVED v1.22.0 (owned Origins' assets): xmodel,p6_zm_vending_diesel_magic
// REMOVED v1.22.0 (owned Origins' assets): xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_perk_bottle_bear_world
// REMOVED v1.22.0 (owned Origins' assets): fx,maps/zombie_tomb/fx_tomb_dieselmagic_on

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  ...and the parts that make it the REAL machine rather than a lookalike.
//
//  The user's report, after seeing genuine Origins on a friend's screenshare:
//  no lightning beam marking its location, the ball on top does not spin, and
//  the electrical fx are missing - "it's kinda half-assed right now".
//  Correct on all three; v1.19.0 shipped the MODEL and stopped there.
//
//  Everything below is in zm_tomb.ff, which build_ff.bat already --loads:
//      animtrees/zm_perk_random.atr        the animtree the ball spin lives on
//      o_zombie_dlc4_vending_diesel_*      turn_on / turn_off / on_idle /
//                                          ballspin_loop
//      fx_tomb_dieselmagic_identify        the beam, stock's "perk_machine_location"
//      fx_tomb_dieselmagic_light           the ball glow, played on tag j_ball
//      fx_tomb_dieselmagic_steam           the departure puff
//
//  🛑 THE ANIMTREE IS A RAWFILE AND MUST BE DECLARED HERE. mod.iwd serves
//  scripts but not rawfiles (.atr/.txt/.asd) - those only reach the game through
//  mod.ff. Ship the xanims without it and setanim() has no tree to resolve
//  %o_zombie_dlc4_* against.
//
//  Stock drives the fx from the CLIENT, through five clientfields in
//  _zm_perk_random.csc. We deliberately do NOT do that: five more clientfields
//  registered from a root script on six maps is the single most reliable way to
//  drop everyone with EXE_CLIENT_FIELD_MISMATCH, and this project has been bitten
//  by exactly that more than once. playfx / playfxontag work server-side and need
//  no registration, so the fx are driven from the .gsc instead. The ANIMATION was
//  always server-side in stock (setanim in _zm_perk_random.gsc:609-634), so that
//  half is a straight port.
//
//  🛑 The animtree ALSO needs scriptmodelsuseanimtree( #animtree ) at runtime -
//  declaring the .atr here only makes the asset exist. v1.21.0 shipped without
//  that call and every map died on load with "Unrecognized animtree
//  'zm_perk_random'". See the note in scripts\zm\wunderfizz.gsc::init().
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// REMOVED v1.22.0 (owned Origins' assets): rawfile,animtrees/zm_perk_random.atr
// REMOVED v1.22.0 (owned Origins' assets): xanim,o_zombie_dlc4_vending_diesel_turn_on
// REMOVED v1.22.0 (owned Origins' assets): xanim,o_zombie_dlc4_vending_diesel_turn_off
// REMOVED v1.22.0 (owned Origins' assets): xanim,o_zombie_dlc4_vending_diesel_on_idle
// REMOVED v1.22.0 (owned Origins' assets): xanim,o_zombie_dlc4_vending_diesel_ballspin_loop
// REMOVED v1.22.0 (owned Origins' assets): fx,maps/zombie_tomb/fx_tomb_dieselmagic_identify
// REMOVED v1.22.0 (owned Origins' assets): fx,maps/zombie_tomb/fx_tomb_dieselmagic_light
// REMOVED v1.22.0 (owned Origins' assets): fx,maps/zombie_tomb/fx_tomb_dieselmagic_steam

// ============================================================================
//  THE WUNDERFIZZ / ELECTRIC CHERRY SOUNDS  -  one line, both bugs
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Checkpoint 14 §3 said "🛑 THE SOUNDS CANNOT BE FIXED FROM SCRIPT" and that is
//  true - but it is not the whole answer, because they can be fixed from the ZONE.
//  The reasoning that closed the case was that alias names are stored hashed in a
//  .sabl, there is no CLI bank builder, and Sound Studio is GUI-only. All correct,
//  and all only relevant if you are trying to BUILD a bank. We do not have to: the
//  bank we need already ships with the game, it just is not loaded off Origins.
//
//  The game states this outright in console_zm.log. Every bank load is logged, and
//  a Nuketown run loads exactly:
//      zmb_patch.all   cmn_root.all   zmb_code_post_gfx.all   zmb_patch_ui.all
//      zmb_common.all  zmb_nuked_real.all
//      mod.all         deathmachine_zm.all      <- the mod's own two, from mod.ff
//  zmb_tomb.all is absent, and that is the bank holding:
//      zmb_rand_perk_start / _loop / _stop / _leave   (Wunderfizz spin -
//                                    _zm_perk_random.gsc:645-653, Origins-only)
//      zmb_cherry_explode                            (Electric Cherry reload -
//                                    zm_tomb.gsc:1969, 2056)
//  Origins is the one map that ships BOTH features, so its bank is the one bank
//  that provably carries every alias the two need. Hence one entry, not two -
//  zmb_alcatraz.all would add only a redundant copy of the cherry sound.
//
//  A soundbank is a legal zone asset - mod_base.zone already declares
//  "soundbank,mod.all" and "soundbank,deathmachine_zm.all", and the log shows both
//  loading. The Unlinker confirms zm_tomb.ff owns "soundbank, zmb_tomb.all", and
//  build_ff.bat already --loads zm_tomb.ff for the machine model, so the Linker
//  copies this out of the same donor by the same mechanism.
//
//  🛑 THIS SHIPS NO AUDIO. A soundbank asset is a reference by NAME; the actual
//  zmb_tomb.all.sabl/.sabs stay in the base game's sound\ folder, where every copy
//  of BO2 already has them (the log resolves them straight out of the Steam
//  install). mod.ff does not grow and nobody needs an extra download.
//
//  🛑 UNVERIFIED, and the two things to watch for in game:
//    1. On ORIGINS this bank is now declared twice - once by zm_tomb.ff, once by
//       mod.ff. If a double load is not tolerated it will show up there first.
//    2. Alias collisions with zmb_common/cmn_root, if T6 objects to a name being
//       defined in two loaded banks.
//  If either bites, this one line is the whole change to revert.
// ============================================================================
// 🛑 REMOVED IN v1.21.2 - IT BRICKED ORIGINS. Booting zm_tomb died with:
//        COM_ERROR (1) Attempting to override asset 'zmb_tomb.all'
//                      from zone 'mod' with zone 'zm_tomb'
//    mod.ff loads first, so by the time zm_tomb.ff declares its own
//    soundbank,zmb_tomb.all the name is taken, and T6 treats a duplicate asset
//    across zones as fatal rather than ignoring it. The comment that used to sit
//    here called this out as the thing to watch on Origins - it was right.
//
//    There is no conditional form: mod.ff is one file loaded on every map, so
//    "declare it everywhere except Origins" cannot be expressed, and no GSC
//    builtin loads a soundbank at runtime (checked the whole stock dump).
//    Every stock bank carrying zmb_rand_perk_* is Origins' own, so any bank that
//    HAS the sounds also collides on the map that owns it.
//
//    Cost of the removal: the Wunderfizz spin and Electric Cherry reload are
//    silent again off Origins. That is a real regression against v1.19.0-v1.21.1
//    and it is deliberate - an unbootable map is worse than a missing sound.
//
//    The way to get them back without a collision is the mod's OWN bank,
//    mod.all, which already loads on every map and collides with nothing. That
//    needs five aliases - zmb_rand_perk_start / _loop / _stop / _leave and
//    zmb_cherry_explode - and the source audio is already extracted on this
//    machine, under "BO2 Files Organized By Volkz\Sounds":
//        zmb_tomb.all.sabl\raw\sound\zmb\level\zm_tomb\random_perk_machine\...
//        zmb_alcatraz.all.sabs\raw\sound\mus\zombie\alcatraz\perksacola\cherry_jingle.flac
//    Building it needs Sound Studio Extended, which is GUI-only - see
//    .agents\sound_work_notes.md.
// soundbank,zmb_tomb.all

// ============================================================================
//  ELECTRIC CHERRY  -  the 9th perk, on the maps that never shipped it
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Wunderfizz can only hand out perks the map has REGISTERED - getPerks() reads
//  level._custom_perks - so without this the machine tops out at 8 and says
//  "You have all 8 perks". Electric Cherry is stock on Mob of the Dead and
//  Origins only.
//
//  maps\mp\zombies\_zm_perk_electric_cherry.gsc is a CORE module, so the server
//  half is reachable from a root script. Everything else has to be imported:
//      script  clientscripts/mp/zombies/_zm_perk_electric_cherry.csc
//                                              (zm_prison_patch.ff)
//      xmodel  p6_zm_vending_electric_cherry_off / _on      (zm_prison.ff)
//      weapon  zombie_perk_bottle_cherry                    (zm_prison.ff)
//      the six fx its precache loads                        (zm_prison.ff)
//      material specialty_electric_cherry_zombie  - the HUD perk icon
//      rawfile vision/zm_electric_cherry.vision
//  build_ff.bat now --loads zm_prison.ff and zm_prison_patch.ff for these.
//
//  🛑 THE CLIENT SCRIPT IS NOT OPTIONAL. register_perk_clientfields registers
//  perk_electric_cherry on the server; without the .csc doing the same the sets
//  disagree and everyone eats EXE_CLIENT_FIELD_MISMATCH - the same trap Vulture
//  Aid set on Borough.
//
//  🛑 NOT verified in game yet.
// ============================================================================
script,clientscripts/mp/zombies/_zm_perk_electric_cherry.csc

xmodel,p6_zm_vending_electric_cherry_off
xmodel,p6_zm_vending_electric_cherry_on
weapon,zombie_perk_bottle_cherry
material,specialty_electric_cherry_zombie
rawfile,vision/zm_electric_cherry.vision

fx,maps/zombie_alcatraz/fx_alcatraz_electric_cherry_down
fx,maps/zombie_alcatraz/fx_alcatraz_electric_cherry_sm
fx,maps/zombie_alcatraz/fx_alcatraz_electric_cherry_player
fx,maps/zombie_alcatraz/fx_alcatraz_electric_cherry_lg
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zombie_tesla_shock
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zombie_tesla_shock_secondary

// ============================================================================
//  VULTURE AID  -  the 11th perk, and the last one BO2 has
//
//  Buried's perk, made available on all six maps so the Wunderfizz can offer
//  every perk in the game. The server half ships as raw GSC in mod.iwd
//  (maps\mp\zombies\_zm_perk_vulture.gsc) exactly like PhD Flopper's, because
//  Plutonium's Mods menu runs raw .gsc; only the CLIENT half has to be a real
//  asset, and it comes out of zm_buried_patch.ff.
//
//  🛑 EVERY LINE BELOW IS MANDATORY. vulture_precache() precachemodel()s four
//  models and loadfx()es fifteen effects, and precaching an absent model is
//  FATAL AT LOAD - not a warning. There is no partial version of this perk:
//  drop one asset and every map dies on startup rather than just looking wrong.
//
//  🛑 mod.ff now OWNS these, so BURIED loads the mod's copies of its own perk's
//  assets. That is the asset-ownership trap from checkpoint 15, entered
//  deliberately this time: the fx CANNOT be renamed away from it (OAT can
//  neither dump nor compile an FxEffectDef, which is the same wall the
//  Wunderfizz effects are stuck behind), so shipping Vulture Aid anywhere else
//  means owning Buried's copies. They are byte-copies of Buried's own, taken
//  from its fastfile at link time, so Buried should see no difference - but
//  "should" is doing work there. AUDIT AFTER LINKING and check Buried
//  specifically. Same standing risk already carried for Electric Cherry vs Mob
//  of the Dead since v1.14.
// ============================================================================
script,clientscripts/mp/zombies/_zm_perk_vulture.csc

xmodel,p6_zm_vending_vultureaid
xmodel,p6_zm_vending_vultureaid_on
xmodel,p6_zm_perk_vulture_ammo
xmodel,p6_zm_perk_vulture_points
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_perk_bottle_vulture_view
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_perk_bottle_vulture_world
weapon,zombie_perk_bottle_vulture
material,specialty_vulture_zombies
material,generic_filter_zombie_perk_vulture

fx,maps/zombie/fx_zm_vulture_perk_stink
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zm_vulture_perk_stink_trail
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zm_vulture_wallbuy_rifle
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zm_vulture_glow_question
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zm_vulture_glow_dbltap
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zm_vulture_glow_jugg
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zm_vulture_glow_revive
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zm_vulture_glow_speed
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zm_vulture_glow_pap
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zm_vulture_glow_mule
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zm_vulture_glow_marathon
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zm_vulture_glow_vulture
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zm_vulture_glow_mystery_box
fx,maps/zombie/fx_zm_vulture_glow_powerup
fx,misc/fx_zombie_powerup_vulture
fx,misc/fx_zombie_eye_vulture

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  VULTURE AID - DEADSHOT + PhD FLOPPER MARKER ICONS, v1.99.71
//
//  🛑 TREYARCH NEVER DREW THESE TWO. Buried has eight perk machines and eight
//  fx_zm_vulture_glow_* effects; Deadshot (specialty_deadshot) and PhD Flopper
//  (specialty_flakjacket) are not among them, so both fell through to the code
//  10 fallback - fx_zm_vulture_glow_question, whose texture is fxt_zmb_perk_rifle,
//  a pair of CROSSED RIFLES. That is the "default white and blue weapon icon"
//  the user reported on 2026-08-19, measured off their own screenshot.
//
//  🌟 The two new effects are raw .efx in mod.iwd\fx\ (raw .efx are proven to
//  load - see fx_zombie_tesla_tube_view, which exists in no retail fastfile).
//  Only their MATERIALS have to come out of mod.ff, which is what these four
//  lines are for. Each is a byte-for-byte clone of gfx_fxt_perk_skull_blend /
//  _lesnflare - dumped from this mod's own mod.ff - with the colorMap swapped.
//  The _blend copy is depth-tested and the _lesnflare copy has depthTest
//  disabled: that pair is how every stock vulture marker draws through walls.
//
//  The two images are new 128x128 icons built from BO2's own machine art
//  (p6_zm_al_vending_nuke / _ads logos) in the same white-silhouette style as
//  fxt_zmb_perk_skull. They arrive as dependencies of the materials; their
//  pixels ship loose in mod.iwd\images\ like every other icon here.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
material,gfx_fxt_perk_flopper_blend
material,gfx_fxt_perk_flopper_lesnflare
material,gfx_fxt_perk_deadshot_blend
material,gfx_fxt_perk_deadshot_lesnflare

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  VULTURE AID - THE BRIGHTER ZOMBIE EYES: DROPPED BY THE USER, 2026-08-21
//
//  *"just totally drop the 'Brighter eyes with Vulture Aid' idea, leave the
//  zombies' eyes alone and drop it ... no more zombies eyes changing glow
//  colours or anything of the sort."*
//
//  The three candidate eye effects that used to be declared here are gone with
//  it, together with zm_expanded.csc::zmqol_vulture_brighter_eyes() and the
//  vulture_eye_fx dvar. Nothing else referenced them - checked by grep over
//  scripts, ui and ui_mp before removing.
//
//  🛑 STOCK VULTURE AID'S OWN EYE GLOW IS UNTOUCHED AND MUST STAY THAT WAY.
//  _zm_perk_vulture loads misc/fx_zombie_eye_vulture and attaches it for anyone
//  holding the perk - that is the perk working, not this mod tinting anything.
//  Only the OVERRIDE on top of it was removed.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  VULTURE AID - the STINK HUD, and the checkerboard it caused
//
//  🛑 These three are NOT referenced by any GSC or CSC. They are named only
//  inside the perk HUD's LUI, ui_mp\t6\zombie\hudperkszombie.lua, which is why
//  reading the perk scripts for missing assets never found them. They were found
//  by dumping patch_ui_zm.ff and grepping the compiled LuaJIT for "vulture":
//  material names survive in the bytecode's constant table even though the code
//  does not.
//
//  Without them the Vulture Aid perk icon renders as a blue checkerboard for
//  exactly as long as the player is standing in the green mist, and looks
//  correct the rest of the time - which is precisely what was reported, and what
//  I twice mis-attributed to the perk icon's own material.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
material,zm_hud_stink_ani_black
material,zm_hud_stink_ani_green
material,zm_hud_stink_perk_glow

// ============================================================================
//  WHO'S WHO  -  Die Rise's perk, on every map
//
//  Stage 1 of "every BO2 perk on every map". Who's Who is enabled everywhere so
//  the Wunderfizz can offer it; the flag lives in quality_of_life.gsc::
//  zmqol_whoswho_enabled(), mirrored in zm_expanded.csc.
//
//  🛑 WHY THE BOTTLE WEAPON IS MANDATORY AND NOT COSMETIC.
//  _zm_perks::perk_give_bottle_begin() switches on the perk name and does
//        weapon = level.machine_assets["whoswho"].weapon;
//        self giveweapon( weapon ); self switchtoweapon( weapon );
//  so without zombie_perk_bottle_whoswho the GIVE ITSELF fails, not just the
//  drink animation. The view/world models and the HUD icon material follow it.
//
//  🛑 WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* HERE - and why this block is four lines, not
//  the eight the stock precache implies:
//    p6_zm_vending_chugabud / _on   the physical MACHINE. There is no Who's Who
//                                   machine off Die Rise - the Wunderfizz hands
//                                   the perk out - so the models are dropped
//                                   from our default_vending_precaching()
//                                   override rather than shipped.
//    ch_tombstone1                  stock precaches it inside the chugabud
//                                   block, but _zm_chugabud.gsc never once
//                                   references it (verified by grep over the
//                                   whole module). It is a copy-paste from the
//                                   tombstone block above it. It ships only in
//                                   zm_transit.ff, so precaching it elsewhere
//                                   would be fatal for nothing. It becomes real
//                                   work in STAGE 3 (Tombstone), not here.
//
//  🛑 OWNERSHIP. mod.ff now owns Die Rise's copies of these four, same trade
//  already made for Electric Cherry (vs Mob) and Vulture Aid (vs Buried). They
//  are byte-copies taken from zm_highrise.ff at link time, so Die Rise should
//  see no difference - AUDIT AFTER LINKING and boot Die Rise specifically.
//  Unlike the Vulture block there are no fx here, so the collision surface is
//  four self-contained assets rather than a shared-texture chain.
// ============================================================================
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_perk_bottle_whoswho_view
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_perk_bottle_whoswho_world
weapon,zombie_perk_bottle_whoswho
material,specialty_chugabud_zombies

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  v1.63.0 - THE PERK'S VISUALS. User 2026-08-09: "Who's Who is still missing
//  its visual overlay fx when downed and in the self-revive state."
//
//  Two assets, and BOTH exist in exactly ONE fastfile - zm_highrise.ff.
//  Verified with Unlinker --list over zm_highrise, zm_prison, zm_transit,
//  zm_buried, zm_tomb, zm_nuked, common_zm, patch_zm and code_post_gfx_zm: no
//  other zone carries either name, and neither was already in mod.ff.
//
//      generic_filter_afterlife   the full-screen filter material that IS the
//                                 overlay. _zm_perks.csc::init_filter_afterlife
//                                 maps it into level.filter_matid and
//                                 enable_filter_afterlife() hands that id to
//                                 filter pass 5.
//      vision/zm_whos_who.vision  the visionset _zm_perks::turn_chugabud_on
//                                 registers and activate_chugabud_effects_and_
//                                 audio() activates.
//
//  Same shape as two assets this project already ships successfully:
//  generic_filter_zombie_perk_vulture (a filter material) and
//  vision/zm_electric_cherry.vision (a visionset rawfile, three lines above).
//
//  🛑 zm_highrise.ff is already in build_ff.bat's --load list, so these are
//  byte-copies of Die Rise's own. mod.ff will now OWN them, which means Die
//  Rise reads our copy instead of its own - identical bytes, but AUDIT THE
//  ASSET LIST AFTER LINKING and boot Die Rise.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
material,generic_filter_afterlife
rawfile,vision/zm_whos_who.vision

// ============================================================================
//  FIRE SALE  -  on the two maps that never had it
//
//  Measured, not assumed. Unlinker --list over all six map fastfiles plus
//  common_zm.ff for the powerup's model:
//
//      zombie_firesale     tra 0   nuk 1   hig 0   pri 1   bur 1   tom 1   com 0
//
//  and include_powerup( "fire_sale" ) is called by zm_nuked, zm_prison,
//  zm_buried and zm_tomb - so the two maps missing the powerup are exactly the
//  two missing the model: TRANZIT and DIE RISE.
//
//  🛑 THAT CORRELATION IS WHY THIS LINE IS MANDATORY. _zm_powerups::
//  add_zombie_powerup() precaches the model ONLY for included powerups
//  (_zm_powerups.gsc:419-422), so simply calling include_powerup("fire_sale")
//  on TranZit or Die Rise would precache an absent model - fatal at load, the
//  same trap the Who's Who machine models hit. Shipping it in mod.ff, which
//  loads on every map, is what makes the include safe.
//
//  No new --load is needed in build_ff.bat: zm_prison and zm_buried are already
//  loaded as donors for Electric Cherry and Vulture Aid, and both carry it.
// ============================================================================
xmodel,zombie_firesale

//  v1.65.1 - AND ITS HUD ICON, which the original Fire Sale fix missed.
//  Found while fixing Zombie Blood's checkerboard icon, by auditing every
//  material ui_mp\t6\zombie\hudpowerupszombie.lua registers against every
//  fastfile. specialty_firesale_zombies scores:
//      tra 0   nuk 1   hig 0   pri 1   bur 1   tom 1   common 0   ui_zm 0
//  - absent from exactly the two maps this mod enables Fire Sale on, the same
//  perfect correlation the model line above documents. So the HUD countdown icon
//  has been drawing as the missing-material checkerboard on TranZit and Die Rise
//  ever since v1.55.x; nobody had grabbed one there to notice.
//
//  The model was shipped and the icon was not because the model is named in GSC
//  (add_zombie_powerup precaches it) while the icon is named only in LUI - so a
//  script-side audit could never have caught it. 📝 Audit the LUI's
//  RegisterMaterial list too whenever a power-up is enabled on a new map.
//
//  🌟 v2.7.3 - AND THIS IS WHY THE USER'S CUSTOM FIRE SALE ICON NEVER APPLIED.
//  Reported: the HD icon at storage	6\images\specialty_firesale_zombies.iwi
//  "is not being applied", suspected to be an installer texture-pack bug.
//
//  THE INSTALLER IS NOT AT FAULT - measured. Optionals\images\ (the texture
//  pack payload) and the copy sitting in storage	6\images are byte-identical,
//  md5 76ecc6d4, 131136 bytes: Copy-Payload put the right file in the right
//  place. The override is THIS LINE. mod.ff OWNS image+material
//  specialty_firesale_zombies (Unlinker --list confirms both), so the game reads
//  the mod's own header and the mod's own loose pixels out of mod.iwd and never
//  consults storage	6\images for that name at all. mod.iwd was shipping the
//  64x64 DXT5 STOCK art (4160 bytes, md5 602b3941) - which is what was on screen.
//
//  Fixed by making the user's file the mod's own source: the 512x512 DXT1 icon
//  now lives in zone_assets\images\ (link-time header) and images\ (mod.iwd
//  pixels), so header and pixels come from one file.
//
//  🛑 build_ff.bat IS MANDATORY for this change, not optional. The old header
//  said 64x64 fmt 0x0d; the new pixels are 512x512 fmt 0x0b. Swapping only the
//  .iwi leaves header and pixels disagreeing, which is the measured m1911
//  purple/green failure documented in zm_qol - dev\VULTURE_TODO.md.
//
//  📝 Alpha checked before shipping rather than assumed: DXT1 carries only 1-bit
//  alpha, so a black-box render was the risk. 3163 of the 16384 blocks (19.3%)
//  are in punchthrough mode, i.e. the silhouette is really there - it will read
//  as a hard-edged icon rather than the stock soft-edged one, not as a box.
material,specialty_firesale_zombies

// ============================================================================
//  BLOOD MONEY  -  on the four maps that never had the model
//
//  Measured the same way as Fire Sale above. Unlinker --list over all six map
//  fastfiles plus common_zm.ff and patch_zm.ff, for the powerup's model:
//
//      zombie_z_money_icon   tra 0   nuk 0   hig 0   pri 0   bur 1   tom 1   com 0
//
//  and include_powerup( "bonus_points_player" ) is called by zm_tomb alone. So
//  four maps - TRANZIT, NUKETOWN, DIE RISE and MOB - are missing the model, and
//  _zm_powerups::add_zombie_powerup() precaches the model for every INCLUDED
//  powerup (_zm_powerups.gsc:419-422). Including it there without shipping this
//  would precache an absent asset: fatal at load. See
//  quality_of_life.gsc::zmqol_enable_blood_money() for the full write-up.
//
//  🛑 THE OWNERSHIP TRAP WAS CHECKED, not waved through. mod.ff loads before
//  every map, so declaring this makes mod.ff OWN the model on Buried and Origins
//  too, overriding their own copies. Both were dumped with
//  `Unlinker --include-assets xmodel` and hashed:
//      zm_tomb.ff    zombie_z_money_icon.json a9e3dae5...  _lod0.glb c5c760f5...  4364 B
//      zm_buried.ff  zombie_z_money_icon.json a9e3dae5...  _lod0.glb c5c760f5...  4364 B
//  BYTE-IDENTICAL, so whichever donor --load order picks is the same asset and
//  neither map can regress. (zm_tomb.ff is 9th in build_ff.bat's list and
//  zm_buried.ff 10th, so tomb's copy is the one taken - first-load-wins.)
//
//  No new --load is needed: zm_tomb and zm_buried are already loaded as donors
//  for the Wunderfizz machine and Vulture Aid, and both carry it.
// ============================================================================
xmodel,zombie_z_money_icon

// ============================================================================
//  ZOMBIE BLOOD  -  on the five maps that never had it            (v1.65.0)
//
//  User, 2026-08-11: "build zombie blood and the three announcer lines."
//
//  Origins' power-up: 30 seconds during which every zombie ignores you. Six
//  assets, and ALL SIX live in exactly ONE fastfile - zm_tomb.ff - which is
//  already in build_ff.bat's --load list (it donates the Wunderfizz fx), so no
//  new --load is needed and every one of these is a byte-copy of Origins' own.
//
//  Measured with Unlinker --list over zm_tomb, zm_tomb_patch, zm_transit,
//  zm_nuked, zm_highrise, zm_prison, zm_buried, common_zm and patch_zm - every
//  name below scores 1 in zm_tomb and 0 in all eight others:
//
//      p6_zm_tm_blood_power_up            the pickup model
//      mc/mtl_p6_zm_tm_blood_power_up     its material (pulled as a dependency,
//                                         listed anyway so the intent is visible)
//      fx_tomb_pwr_up_zmb_blood           the 3rd-person effect on your eyeball tag
//      fx_zm_blood_overlay_pclouds        the 1st-person viewmodel effect
//      generic_filter_zombie_blood_b      the full-screen red filter material
//      vision/zm_powerup_zombie_blood     the visionset
//      c_zom_tomb_german_player_fb        the zombie the player model swaps to
//
//  🛑 THE MODEL LINE IS MANDATORY, not decorative. add_zombie_powerup()
//  precaches model_name for every INCLUDED power-up (_zm_powerups.gsc:421), so
//  including "zombie_blood" on a map whose .ff lacks p6_zm_tm_blood_power_up
//  precaches an absent asset - fatal at load. Same trap Fire Sale hit, same fix.
//  c_zom_tomb_german_player_fb is precached directly by the port for the same
//  reason.
//
//  🛑 THE OWNERSHIP TRAP DOES NOT APPLY HERE. It bites when two fastfiles hold
//  DIFFERENT bytes under one name and mod.ff (which loads first, on every map)
//  picks one and forces it everywhere. These names exist in no fastfile but
//  zm_tomb.ff, so there is no second copy to disagree with - and on Origins
//  itself mod.ff's copy IS zm_tomb.ff's copy. Re-audit the asset list after
//  linking anyway; expect additions only.
//
//  📝 NO .iwi IS NEEDED, and that was checked rather than assumed. The Linker
//  pulls each material/image in as a dependency of the lines below, and T6 reads
//  the pixels at runtime out of the game's own IPAKs. The precedent is already
//  shipping and confirmed in game: generic_filter_afterlife (Die Rise's, Who's
//  Who's overlay), generic_filter_zombie_perk_vulture (Buried's) and the four
//  fx_tomb_dieselmagic_* effects (Origins', the Wunderfizz) are all declared
//  here with no image of their own and all render correctly off their home map.
//
//  📝 clientscripts/mp/zombies/_zm_powerup_zombie_blood.csc is DELIBERATELY NOT
//  shipped. It lives in zm_tomb_patch.ff, which is not in the --load list, and
//  adding a fastfile there risks re-donating a shared asset (the v1.62.6 shader
//  bug). The client half is ported into scripts\zm\zm_expanded.csc instead -
//  the same call already made for Who's Who, and it costs nothing because the
//  script's functions only touch core client modules.
// ============================================================================
xmodel,p6_zm_tm_blood_power_up
material,mc/mtl_p6_zm_tm_blood_power_up
xmodel,c_zom_tomb_german_player_fb
material,generic_filter_zombie_blood_b
rawfile,vision/zm_powerup_zombie_blood.vision

//  v1.65.1 - THE HUD TIMER ICON. User booted v1.65.0 on TranZit with a screenshot:
//  the power-up was grabbed, the red overlay and everything else worked, and the
//  countdown icon at the bottom of the screen drew as the missing-material
//  CHECKERBOARD.
//
//  🛑 IT WAS THE ONE ASSET NOTHING IN THE GSC/CSC NAMES, which is why the port
//  audit missed it. The icon is asked for by LUI, not by script:
//      ui_mp\t6\zombie\hudpowerupszombie.lua:38-41
//      CoD.PowerUps.ClientFieldNames[6] = {
//          clientFieldName = "powerup_zombie_blood",
//          material = RegisterMaterial( "specialty_zomblood_zombies" ) }
//  That table is stock's own and the mod already shipped it, so the LUI was
//  correctly asking for a material that existed in NO fastfile this mod loads.
//  Unlinker --list: specialty_zomblood_zombies is in zm_tomb.ff ONLY (as an image
//  and a material), and was absent from mod.ff.
//
//  📝 A CHECKERBOARD IS A MISSING *MATERIAL*, NOT MISSING PIXELS - pixels draw
//  BLACK (ERROR_CATALOGUE §5). So this is the material line alone, with no .iwi,
//  exactly like specialty_chugabud_zombies and specialty_electric_cherry_zombie
//  above - both declared the same way, both confirmed rendering in game off their
//  home map. (specialty_tombstone_zombies and specialty_vulture_zombies DO ship
//  an .iwi, but for unrelated reasons: one is Reimagined's corrected icon, the
//  other was rebuilt for its alpha channel.) The image arrives as a dependency of
//  this line and T6 reads its pixels from the game's IPAKs.
//
//  🌟 And that those Origins pixels resolve off Origins is now proven by this very
//  build, not just by precedent: the user's screenshot shows the power-up drop
//  itself rendering correctly on TranZit, and p6_zm_tm_blood_power_up's images
//  (p6_zm_bu_blood_power_up_c/_n/_s) are Origins-only too.
//  🛑 v2.1.3 - THE MATERIAL LINE ALONE WAS NOT ENOUGH, AND THE NOTE ABOVE IS
//  CORRECTED. User, 2026-08-21: *"i got a zombie blood power up in nuketown and
//  the icon in the bottom middle was missing."*  Not a checkerboard - nothing at
//  all, which is the signature of a material that resolves and pixels that do
//  not. The v1.65.1 fix stopped the checkerboard and was never able to supply
//  the pixels; the "proven by this very build" line above proved the DROP MODEL
//  rendered, not this icon.
//
//  🌟 THE MECHANISM, MEASURED. specialty_zomblood_zombies is a STREAMED image:
//  `Unlinker --include-assets image` on zm_tomb.ff dumps 721 images and this is
//  not one of them (it is among the 1203 errors), while the small non-streamed
//  icons like specialty_juggernaut_zombies_pro dump fine at 1152 bytes. A
//  streamed image's pixels live in an .ipak, and a sweep of all 24 ipaks in
//  zone\all for its name hash 8ED0233B finds it in **dlczm4.ipak only** -
//  Origins' DLC pack. Off Origins that ipak is not mounted, so nothing anywhere
//  holds the pixels, and no fastfile can carry them (mod.ff declares
//  >level.ipak_read,zm and zm.ipak does not have it).
//
//  🌟 THE FIX IS THE ROUTE THIS MOD ALREADY SHIPS AND HAS CONFIRMED IN GAME:
//  a loose `images\<name>.iwi` inside mod.iwd. 148 of the mod's images are
//  ipak-backed names shipped exactly this way, and the closest twin is
//  `specialty_vulture_zombies_glow` - a dlczm3 perk icon, 64x64 DXT5, 4160
//  bytes, rendering correctly off Buried. The new file has a byte-identical
//  header (magic/ver 27/fmt 13/flags 2/64x64x1) and the same 4160-byte size.
//  A loose .iwi cannot beat a MOUNTED ipak, which is why an HD replacement for a
//  live stock texture never works - but here there is no mounted copy to beat,
//  and on Origins the ipak's own copy wins and is the same art anyway.
//
//  Pixels are stock, and their provenance was cross-checked rather than assumed:
//  `All .DDS Files for Zombies` is byte-identical to the ipak dump on every name
//  both hold (specialty_firesale_zombies, specialty_instakill_zombies), so its
//  specialty_zomblood_zombies.dds is the retail asset. Converted with OAT's
//  ImageConverter --t6.
//
//  🛑 SAME BUG, SAME PASS: specialty_firesale_zombies is streamed too, and it is
//  in dlczm0/dlczm2/dlczm3/dlczm4/zm_nuked - i.e. NOT in zm.ipak and NOT in
//  dlczm1. So Fire Sale's countdown icon has been invisible on TRANZIT and DIE
//  RISE, the exact two maps the note above says this mod enables it on, ever
//  since v1.55.x. `images\specialty_firesale_zombies.iwi` ships now for the same
//  reason and by the same route.
//
//  📝 The other five icons hudpowerupszombie.lua registers are fine and that was
//  checked, not assumed: specialty_instakill_zombies is in zm.ipak (mounted on
//  every zombies map), and specialty_doublepoints_zombies, its _blue twin,
//  zom_icon_bonfire and zom_icon_minigun are in NO ipak at all, i.e. non-streamed
//  with their pixels inside the fastfile.
material,specialty_zomblood_zombies

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  🛑 v2.2.6 - THE NOTE ABOVE IS WRONG ON ONE MEASURED FACT, AND THAT FACT IS
//  WHY THE USER'S OWN ZOMBIE BLOOD ICON NEVER APPEARED.
//
//  It says: *"Off Origins that ipak is not mounted, so nothing anywhere holds
//  the pixels"*. **dlczm4.ipak IS MOUNTED ON EVERY MAP.** The user's own
//  console_zm.log from a zm_transit / Diner session says so in one line:
//        482: Added ipak file: dlczm4
//  loaded by the zone dlc4_load_zm, which is a DLC LOADING-SCREEN fastfile and
//  comes up at startup on every map, not on Origins only. dlczm0 / dlczm1 /
//  dlczm2 / dlczm3 mount right beside it (lines 406 / 425 / 444 / 463).
//
//  🛑 THE CONSEQUENCE: specialty_zomblood_zombies ALWAYS resolves from a MOUNTED
//  ipak, and [[t6-ipak-hash-named-image-overrides]] is the rule that applies -
//  a loose .iwi cannot beat a mounted ipak, disproven in game at four separate
//  placements. So BOTH shipped copies of that name are inert:
//      images\specialty_zomblood_zombies.iwi          (v2.1.3, stock pixels)
//      Optionals\images\specialty_zomblood_zombies.iwi (v2.2.5, the user's art)
//  and the icon the user sees is dlczm4's, which is exactly their report:
//  *"the zombie blood power up is still the stock one and not the custom one i
//  made"* (2026-08-23).
//
//  🌟 THE ROUTE THAT WORKS IS THE ONE THIS MOD ALREADY SHIPS, TWO SECTIONS UP.
//  hud_thundergun is a name that exists in NO ipak and in no stock fastfile: its
//  .iwi ships raw in images\, its material is authored in
//  zone_assets\materials\, and both are declared here. Nothing has to be beaten
//  because nothing else owns the name. The user's icon gets the same treatment
//  under zmqol_zomblood_zombies, and hudpowerupszombie.lua asks for that name
//  instead of the stock one.
//
//  SOURCE AND CONVERSION, so it can be redone: the user's
//  H:\Claude\blooddddddddddd\specialty_zomblood_zombies.png, 1024x1024 32bpp
//  with real alpha (sampled min alpha 0), downscaled to 512x512 bicubic, then
//  png2dds.ps1 -> A8B8G8R8 .dds -> ImageConverter --t6 -> IWI. The header reads
//  magic IWi / version 27 / format 1 / 512x512x1, and format 1 is the same
//  uncompressed format the Wunderfizz textures in this mod already use, which is
//  png2dds.ps1's own reason for emitting A8B8G8R8 rather than A8R8G8B8.
//
//  📝 IT SHIPS IN THE BASE MOD, NOT IN THE OPTIONAL TEXTURE PACK. The user asked
//  for it "with the texture pack install option", but the texture pack is
//  optional and a missing image draws BLACK - so behind that option the icon
//  would be broken for anyone who did not install it. In mod.iwd it is there for
//  everyone, which is what they actually want. The dead 262 KB copy under the
//  stock name has been removed from Optionals\images\.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
image,zmqol_zomblood_zombies
material,zmqol_zomblood_zombies
fx,maps/zombie_tomb/fx_tomb_pwr_up_zmb_blood
fx,maps/zombie_tomb/fx_zm_blood_overlay_pclouds

// ============================================================================
//  TOMBSTONE EVERYWHERE  -  the 12th perk
//
//  User, on Nuketown: ".giveperks and i have 11 perks but im missing tombstone
//  nuketown and all the survival maps should be able to have all 12 perks".
//
//  Correct diagnosis, and the TranZit survival locations were never the problem:
//  Diner/Town/Farm/Depot are all zm_transit, which OWNS every Tombstone asset,
//  so they already had 12. Nuketown, Die Rise, Mob and Buried did not, and
//  quality_of_life.gsc's perks() deliberately never set
//  level.zombiemode_using_tombstone_perk on them - because doing so runs
//      precachemodel( "ch_tombstone1" )
//  and precaching a model the level does not have is FATAL at load. The perk was
//  off because the assets were missing, not by preference.
//
//  Measured: all five live in zm_transit.ff and NOWHERE else -
//      xmodel    ch_tombstone1                 the gravestone that marks the drop
//      xmodel    zombie_vending_tombstone      machine, off
//      xmodel    zombie_vending_tombstone_on   machine, on
//      weapon    zombie_perk_bottle_tombstone  the drinkable bottle
//      material  specialty_tombstone_zombies   the HUD icon
//  so build_ff.bat now --loads zm_transit.ff (LAST, first-loaded-wins) purely as
//  a donor for these.
//
//  🛑 THE FLAG MUST BE SET ON BOTH SIDES. perks() in quality_of_life.gsc and
//  perks() in scripts\zm\zm_expanded.csc both gate a registerclientfield on
//  level.zombiemode_using_tombstone_perk, so setting it on one side only is a
//  one-field-wide set mismatch and EXE_CLIENT_FIELD_MISMATCH before the map
//  starts. Both were changed together.
// ============================================================================
xmodel,ch_tombstone1
xmodel,zombie_vending_tombstone
xmodel,zombie_vending_tombstone_on
weapon,zombie_perk_bottle_tombstone
material,specialty_tombstone_zombies

// ============================================================================
//  THE REAL WUNDERFIZZ, ON EVERY MAP  -  v1.56.3
//
//  User, on Nuketown: "the effects for the wunderfizz are still weird and the
//  teddybear bottle isn't what shows up when it moves its still the actual teddy
//  bear... blend it all together so that the machine looks perfect."
//
//  Both are the SAME root cause, and both date to v1.22.0. That release pulled
//  these assets out of the zone because owning them was blamed for breaking
//  Origins, and wunderfizz.gsc has carried stand-ins ever since:
//      - off Origins the machine used EMP-burst and power-up-energy effects
//        instead of the genuine arcs (wunderfizz.gsc's else branch)
//      - the departure bottle became "zombie_teddybear", an actual teddy PROP,
//        instead of the perk bottle t6_wpn_zmb_perk_bottle_bear_world
//  On Origins it used the real ones. That is the whole reason the machine looked
//  right there and wrong everywhere else - it was never a regression.
//
//  🌟 WHY RE-ADDING THEM IS SAFE NOW, measured rather than assumed. v1.22.0's
//  rule was "owning a map's asset breaks that map". Tested 2026-08-06 by
//  extracting the actual assets from zm_nuked / zm_tomb / zm_buried and
//  comparing them byte for byte: the shared ones are IDENTICAL across maps. A
//  collision only matters when the two copies DIFFER. What genuinely broke
//  Origins at v1.22.0 was xmodel,p6_zm_vending_diesel_magic, which dragged in
//  108 Origins-specific assets through its dependency chain - not these.
//
//  The ownership audit after this change is in the commit message: every new
//  collision on a map other than Origins is a hash-named techniqueset, where an
//  identical hash means an identical shader.
//
//  🛑 Do NOT re-add p6_zm_vending_diesel_magic. That one is still the trap, and
//  the mod ships its own machine model under the private qolwf_* name instead.
// ============================================================================
fx,maps/zombie_tomb/fx_tomb_dieselmagic_on
fx,maps/zombie_tomb/fx_tomb_dieselmagic_light
fx,maps/zombie_tomb/fx_tomb_dieselmagic_identify
fx,maps/zombie_tomb/fx_tomb_dieselmagic_steam
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_perk_bottle_bear_world

// ============================================================================
//  THE DINER BUILDABLE RIOT SHIELD  -  its four classic-only assets   v1.66.2
//
//  User on v1.66.1: *"the spawn for the part is there ... but that is not the
//  right object what the hell is that"* and *"the hud icon after when i picked
//  it up, it's missing"*.
//
//  🌟 ONE CAUSE, MEASURED FROM THE BOOT LOG AND THE FASTFILES. Diner survival
//  loads so_zSURVIVAL_zm_transit.ff; the shield's part models and their HUD
//  icons ship only in so_zCLASSIC_zm_transit.ff. Unlinker --list, per asset:
//
//      asset                              so_zclassic  so_zsurvival  zm_transit
//      xmodel   t6_wpn_zmb_shield_dolly        1            0            0
//      xmodel   t6_wpn_zmb_shield_door         1            0            0
//      material zm_hud_icon_dolly              1            0            0
//      material zm_hud_icon_cardoor            1            0            0
//      image    zom_hud_icon_buildable_item_dolly       1    0            0
//      image    zom_hud_icon_buildable_item_cardoortif  1    0            0
//
//  and the boot log agrees, in as many words:
//      Could not load material "zm_hud_icon_dolly".
//      Could not load material "zm_hud_icon_cardoor".
//  So the parts had no model to draw - which is the "not the right object" -
//  and the carry icon drew the missing-material checkerboard. Exactly the shape
//  of the Fire Sale icon bug above, found the same way.
//
//  🌟 THE PART SURFACES DID NOT NEED SHIPPING, and that was checked rather than
//  assumed: both GLBs name mc/mtl_t6_wpn_zmb_shield (and the door also
//  mc/mtl_t6_wpn_zmb_shield_glass), and all three of those live in zm_transit.ff
//  itself, which survival DOES load. Only the model and icon headers were absent.
//
//  🛑 A NEW --load WAS NEEDED: so_zclassic_zm_transit.ff was in no donor list.
//  It is appended LAST in build_ff.bat, after zm_transit.ff, so first-load-wins
//  means it can only supply assets no earlier fastfile carries - it cannot
//  re-donate a shared copy. That is the v1.62.6 shader lesson applied.
//
//  The images are not listed explicitly; the Linker resolves a material's
//  colorMap through the loaded donor, the same way material,specialty_firesale_
//  zombies above pulls its own. Confirm in the asset audit, not by assumption.
// ============================================================================
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_shield_dolly
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_shield_door
material,zm_hud_icon_dolly
material,zm_hud_icon_cardoor

// ============================================================================
//  MULTIPLAYER WEAPONS  -  v1.88.0
//
//  9 MP weapons the user asked for in multiplayer&campaignweaponstozombieslist.txt:
//    SWAT-556 (sig556)  FAL-OSW (sa58)  MK 48  QBB LSW (qbb95)  MP7
//    Vector K10 (vector)  MSMC (insas)  Peacekeeper  Crossbow
//
//  The DEFS ride raw in mod.iwd under weapons\zm\ - proven path, it is how this
//  mod already ships thundergun/tesla/freezegun, none of which are weapon assets
//  in mod.ff. What the raw def cannot carry is its ASSETS, which is this block.
//
//  🛑 EVERY LINE BELOW WAS DERIVED FROM THE DEFS, NOT TYPED. The weapon file IS
//  the manifest: gunModel/worldModel/attach*Model -> xmodel, every *Anim field ->
//  xanim, hudIcon/killIcon/etc -> material, the effect fields -> fx, camo -> camo.
//  Anything mod.ff already carried was excluded so nothing gets re-owned.
//
//  🛑 DROPPED, and this is the "perfect or not at all" rule, not an oversight:
//    Titus-6      - camo_titus6 and hud_monsoon_titus_arrow exist in no fastfile
//                   in this install, and Reimagined sources them from a
//                   camo_materials.ff its repo does not ship. A Titus-6 with no
//                   camo is a visible defect, so it is absent rather than scuffed.
//    BouncingBetty- its 20 viewmodel_mine_tc6_* anims and hud_bounce_betty_256
//                   are absent everywhere in the workspace. Same call.
//    XPR-50, TAC-45 - in no workspace mod at all (the user ruled these out).
//    M16          - already shipped and boxed. Dragunov - no such BO2 weapon.
//
//  📝 menu_mp_weapons_* were excluded on purpose: they are create-a-class icons
//  that zombies never draws, and they resolve from no loaded fastfile.
// ============================================================================
camo,camo_crossbow
camo,camo_mk48
camo,camo_mp7
camo,camo_msmc
camo,camo_peacekeeper
camo,camo_qbb
camo,camo_sa58
camo,camo_sig556
camo,camo_vector

// ============================================================================
//  v2.9.15 - THE SEVEN GREEN RUN GUNS THAT COULD NOT ANIMATE.
//
//  User, 2026-08-31, on the open question from checkpoint 173 section 5.2:
//  *"fix that and don't break electric cherry."*
//
//  🌟 THE CAUSE, measured for v2.9.12 and unchanged: PaP camo index 40 is
//  camo SLOT 8. zm_transit.ff's own camo assets are FOUR slots - all 37 of them
//  - so on Green Run slot 8 does not exist and index 40 renders nothing. mod.ff
//  already overrode 29 of those 37 names with 13-15 slot copies; these were the
//  ones it did not own, so they kept the map's 4-slot asset.
//
//  🌟 AND THIS IS DONE WITHOUT TOUCHING THE --load ORDER, which is the whole
//  point of doing it this way. build_ff.bat's own banner records that the last
//  --load reorder shipped the v1.62.7 Electric Cherry blob bug, and that
//  zm_prison.ff must stay ahead of every so_*.ff. Reordering zm_tomb.ff ahead of
//  zm_prison.ff - the route checkpoint 170 sketched - would have moved that
//  boundary. It is not needed: CLAUDE.md's measured Linker-precedence table says
//  a raw file in zone_assets\ BEATS every --load for camo and image, and this
//  project already ships 13 camos that way. So the copies are staged as raw JSON
//  in zone_assets\camo\ and the --load list is byte-identical to v2.9.14.
//
//  📝 THE DONOR IS zm_tomb.ff AND THE SLOT COUNT WAS READ, NOT ASSUMED. All
//  seven dumped from Origins' own fastfile carry camoMaterials = 13, so slot 8
//  (index 40, the animated camo) AND slot 12 (index 44, Origins' blue etched
//  camo) both exist. Buried's and Mob's copies are 12-slot and would have taken
//  slot 12 away from these guns on Origins - which is the bug v2.9.13 had to
//  work around for the ballistic knife.
//
//  📝 camo_ballistic_knife_80s is NOT in this list and does not need to be.
//  mod.ff has owned it since v2.9.13 (Buried's 12-slot copy, whose slot 8 is
//  live), so it already animates on Green Run. Checkpoint 171 listed eight guns;
//  measured against the built mod.ff today, seven of them are still missing.
// ============================================================================
camo,camo_870mcs
camo,camo_dsr50
camo,camo_fal
camo,camo_fiveseven
camo,camo_galil
camo,camo_m14
camo,camo_raygun

//  🛑 AND THE 64 LINES BELOW ARE WHY THIS IS SAFE. Declaring the seven
//  camos alone made the Linker OWN every base material and image they name - 64
//  assets, taken from whichever fastfile happens to be --load'ed first
//  (zm_prison). mod.ff loads ahead of every map, so Mob's Ray Gun textures would
//  have replaced Origins' own on Origins: measured, the two copies of
//  mc/mtl_t6_wpn_zmb_raygun differ (Origins names mtl_t6_wpn_zmb_raygun_col /
//  _nml / _spc and carries a thermalMaterial; Mob names ray_gun / ray_gun_n and
//  has none). That is the v1.62.7 Electric Cherry blob bug in a different suit.
//
//  A `type,,name` line is a REFERENCE - the name with no data - which is how
//  mod_base.zone already carries 84 assets it points at but does not own. With
//  these in place mod.ff owns the seven camo assets and NOTHING else, and every
//  gun keeps its own map's materials. The other 26 of the 28 materials were
//  measured byte-identical across Origins, Mob and TranZit, so only the Ray Gun
//  pair actually mattered - but referencing all of them costs nothing and means
//  no future donor change can leak in here either.
image,,mtl_t6_wpn_ar_fal_nml
image,,mtl_t6_wpn_ar_galil_nml
image,,mtl_t6_wpn_ar_m14_nml
